From 8d0b70213e8c741f8fb98fca88645ba60ed083f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:24:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper: Warden stats from one ipset listing, cache replay
 skips populated sets, rtrafd runs tmctl and ping without a shell, the fqdn
 cache is written only when it changed

Four items from the 2026-08-28 efficiency audit (P13, P9, the rtrafd item,
P14); P35a and P30 ride in the previous commits' files.

- rwarden.c rw_gen_stats() (P13): the Warden page's 30 s poll forked one
  `ipset -t list` and one sed per country set inside httpd (~360 processes).
  Now ONE `ipset -t list`, parsed by awk into "<name> <entries>" lines, and
  TN/TN6/GN/GE/GZ are read from that (7 processes). Marker "# stats: one ipset
  -t list for every set".
- rwarden.c rw_gen_apply() (P9): the cache replay in apply.sh re-fed every set
  on every firewall rebuild - up to 800k add-lines into sets that were already
  full on each WAN bounce or Apply. The replay loop takes RWFULL/RWEMPTY from
  one header listing, skips populated sets and logs "cache replay: N set(s)
  already populated, skipped". Boot is unchanged: every set is empty there and
  is replayed. fprintf-emitted shell - no % in that block.
- rtrafd.c rt_exec_bounded(): pipe + fork + execvp, poll() against a
  CLOCK_MONOTONIC deadline, a bounded post-EOF waitpid loop, SIGKILL and
  "rtrafd: %s did not answer in %d s - killed" on timeout. Replaces rt_bound(),
  the four-process shell wrapper (command, watcher subshell, its sleep, wait)
  that seven tmctl queries per 4 s under HW QoS turned into ~7 forks/s, the
  largest Reaper-owned share of an idle box's churn. poll_classes() keeps the
  last reading when a queue answers nothing - no zero that the next poll turns
  into a full-counter spike; the other queues carry on. poll_probe's ping goes
  the same way (host_ok() bounds the characters). rtrafd has no SIGCHLD
  handler. The store windows' monotonic clock (mono_secs: the NTP step expired
  STORE_RETRY_SECS at once and parked a merely late USB store's history as
  .prev) is in the same file.
- reaper_fw.c rfw_gen_resolve() (P14): the fqdn set cache under /jffs is
  rewritten only when `cmp -s` says the members changed - a static list was
  hitting flash 144 times a day per set (busybox CMP=y). Marker "# fqdn cache:
  rewrite only when changed".
- rtrafd/.gitignore: the rc/.gitignore pattern for the build outputs.

Built and verified on RT-BE96U MCP v3.3.3_BETA_r5 (reaper_verify 34/0/0);
QoS class tiles live and no "sleep 3" orphans are the metal asks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
